📘 TOPIC SHEET 5: Power Virtual Agents (PVA) / Copilot Studio
(27 questions — YOUR BIGGEST GAP) ❌ Study from scratch
________________________________________
📖 Concept
Power Virtual Agents (now Microsoft Copilot Studio) lets you build chatbots without code.
Core Architecture
Component	What It Is	Example
Topic	A conversation path (like a dialog)	"Store Hours" topic, "Return Policy" topic
Trigger Phrases	Words/sentences that START a topic	"help", "issue", "trouble" → triggers Support topic
Nodes	Building blocks inside a topic	Question node, Message node, Condition node, Action node
Entities	Data types the bot recognizes	Age, City, Email, Phone, Custom entities
Variables	Store user responses for later use	UserAge = 25, UserName = "Bashar"
Channels	WHERE the bot is published	Teams, Website, Facebook, Custom web channel
Fallback Topic	What happens when bot doesn't understand	"I didn't understand, let me transfer you..."
🧠 Variable Types (EXAM FAVORITE)
Variable Type	Scope	Persists Across Topics?	Use Case
Topic Variable	Single topic only	❌ No	Temp storage within one conversation path
Bot Variable (Global)	Entire bot	✅ Yes	Store name, email across ALL topics
Session Variable	Current session	✅ Yes (within session)	Session-specific data
Exam Rule: If bot needs to maintain info when topic changes → Bot (Global) Variable
Entity Types
Entity Type	What It Does	Example
Pre-built Entities	Microsoft provides them	Age, City, Email, Money, Number, Date, Person name
Closed-list Entity	You define exact values	Product categories: "Laptop", "Phone", "Tablet"
Regular Expression (Regex) Entity	Pattern matching	Order ID format: ORD-####
Smart Matching	Fuzzy matching on closed-list items	User says "Phones" → matches "Phone"
Slot Filling	Auto-fills entity from user's message	"I want a red laptop" → Color=Red, Product=Laptop
________________________________________
🔑 Rules to Memorize
Rule	Remember
1	Bot variable = persists across topics (like global variable)
2	Topic variable = dies when topic ends
3	Trigger phrases = what the user says to START a topic (minimum 5 recommended)
4	Closed-list entity = you define exact values (product categories, departments)
5	Smart matching = fuzzy matching on closed-list (handles typos, plurals)
6	Slot filling = auto-extracts multiple entities from one sentence
7	Channel = where you PUBLISH the bot (Teams, Website, Facebook, etc.)
8	Custom web channel = embed bot on YOUR website using IFrame/code snippet
9	SSO (Single Sign-On) supported in: Teams and Custom website only
10	Publish to entire company in Teams → Submit for admin approval
11	Suggest topics = auto-create topics from existing FAQ/support webpages
12	Testing → use Demo website (built-in test page)
13	Deploy to all users → Share bot with security group
14	Embed in external website → IFrame with bot code
15	Manual authentication = for scenarios requiring user identity (sensitive data)
________________________________________
📝 All Related Questions + Answers
Q172, Q239-240, Q322: Age group chatbot — conditional branches
Scenario: Bot must determine age group (0-17, 18-25, 26-35, 36-55, 55-100)
Solution: Use Age for Identify in the question + add branches with conditional logic
Answer: ✅ Yes — Age is a pre-built entity. Conditional branches check value ranges
How it works:
1.	Ask: "How old are you?" → Identify: Age
2.	Branch: If Age < 18 → "Under 18 group"
3.	Branch: If Age >= 18 AND Age <= 25 → "18-25 group"
4.	... and so on for each group
________________________________________
Q173-174: Variable to maintain info across topics
Scenario: Bot must keep customer name and email when conversation topic changes
Answer: ✅ C. Bot variable (Global variable)
❌ Topic variable — dies when topic ends
❌ Session variable — exists but bot variable is the correct PVA terminology
❌ Slot — slot filling is for entity extraction, not variable storage
Key: "maintain info if topic changes" = always Bot variable
________________________________________
Q175: Custom entities for product categories + variations
Scenario: Teach bot about product categories and variations within categories
•	Product categories (exact list) → Closed-list entity
•	Variations within categories (fuzzy matching) → Smart matching (enabled on closed-list)
Key: Closed-list = you define values. Smart matching = handles synonyms/typos automatically
________________________________________
Q176-177: Create topics from existing website content
Sequence (3 steps):
1.	Suggest topics (Select "Suggest topics" → enter FAQ/support page URLs)
2.	Add suggested topics (review and select which to add)
3.	Enable the topics (toggle them ON)
Key: This is the exact 3-step process. The bot auto-extracts Q&A from web pages
❌ "Identify trigger phrases" is NOT the first step — the system does this automatically
________________________________________
Q243-244: Bot available from Teams AND company website
Answer: ✅ B. Channel
Why: Channels are how you publish a bot to different platforms
•	Teams channel → bot appears in Teams
•	Custom website channel → bot embedded on your site
❌ Template — templates are starting points for bot creation
❌ Skill — skills are reusable bot capabilities (advanced)
❌ Composer — Bot Framework Composer is a pro-dev tool
________________________________________
Q245: Chat solution to answer guest inquiry
Answer: ✅ B (Escalations), C (Smart match), E (Topics)
•	Topics = conversation paths for known questions
•	Smart matching = handles variations of trigger phrases
•	Escalations = transfer to human agent when bot can't help
❌ Variables — store data but don't answer questions
❌ Synonyms — not a PVA component name
________________________________________
Q247-248: Two scenarios — event info + snow conditions
Scenario 1: Guest asks about company event start time
→ Use smart matching to load an entity for a topic (match event name → retrieve info)
Scenario 2: Guest asks about snow conditions
→ Create a fallback topic (weather is external data — bot can't answer, redirect to weather service or escalate)
Key: Known info = topic + smart matching. Unknown/external info = fallback or escalation
________________________________________
Q268: PVA SSO — where can you publish?
Answer: ✅ B (Website with pro-dev tools) and C (Microsoft Teams)
SSO is supported ONLY on:
•	Microsoft Teams
•	Custom websites (using Azure AD authentication)
❌ Mobile app — SSO not natively supported in PVA mobile
❌ Azure Bot Service channels — SSO configuration is different
________________________________________
Q271: Embed PVA in custom website
Answer: ✅ D. Custom web channel
How: PVA generates a code snippet → you embed it in your website's HTML
❌ Webpage URL — not how you embed
❌ Form ID — not relevant
❌ Bot ID — used internally, not for embedding
________________________________________
Q273-274: Permissions for bot creators vs bot users
•	Accounting users (create/collaborate) → Assign Maker permissions (or share bot with edit access)
•	Sales users (chat only) → Share bot with security group (use access only)
Key: Makers = create/edit. Users = chat only via sharing
________________________________________
Q279-280: Testing + Deployment sequence
•	Testing → ✅ Use the demo website (built-in test page, shareable link)
•	Deploy to all users → ✅ Share chatbot to security group containing all users
•	Public website → ✅ Embed chatbot code in IFrame on company's public website
Key: Demo website = testing. Security group = internal deployment. IFrame = external website
________________________________________
Q289: Chatbot security on Power Pages
Answer: ✅ C (Set up new channel) + E (Enable web channel security)
•	Manual authentication (D) = for Entra ID user identification
•	Web channel security = ensures bot is accessible only from authorized domains
❌ Only for Teams auth — too restrictive
❌ DLP policy — controls connectors, not chatbot access
________________________________________
Q304: Environment doesn't appear in PVA
Answer: ✅ C. Create an environment in a supported region
Why: PVA is not available in all regions. If your environment is in an unsupported region, it won't appear
❌ Change region — you can't change an environment's region after creation
❌ Convert to sandbox — doesn't fix region issue
________________________________________
Q305-306: Bot nodes for help desk
•	When user says "issue", "help", "trouble" → Trigger phrases (start the topic)
•	Bot responds "How can we help?" + choices → Question node (with multiple-choice options)
•	Bot saves response for action → Save response to variable
Key: Trigger phrases → Question node → Variable → Action node
________________________________________
Q308-309: Sharing — collaborate vs use only
•	Accounting (collaborate/build) → Share with edit access (co-author)
•	Sales (use only) → Share with view/use access (end user)
Key: PVA has two sharing levels: edit (maker) and use (consumer)
________________________________________
Q312-313: Publish bot to entire company in Teams
Answer: ✅ D. Submit the chatbot for admin approval
Why: To publish a bot company-wide in Teams, you must submit it for tenant admin approval in the Teams admin center
❌ Export/import — not needed within same tenant
❌ Invite teams — doesn't scale to entire company
❌ Email link — not the proper deployment method
❌ Configure Teams channel — this enables Teams, but company-wide requires admin approval
________________________________________
