✅ Exercise 1: Create Your First Bot
1.	Go to https://copilotstudio.microsoft.com (or search "Copilot Studio" in your browser)
2.	Select your environment → + Create a copilot
3.	Name it "PL200 Practice Bot" → Create
4.	You'll see the Topics page with pre-built topics (Greeting, Thank you, etc.)
✅ Exercise 2: Create a Topic with Trigger Phrases
1.	Click + Add a topic → From blank
2.	Name: "Store Hours"
3.	Add trigger phrases: "what are your hours", "when do you open", "store hours", "opening time", "schedule"
4.	Add a Message node: "We're open Mon-Fri 9AM-5PM"
5.	Save → Test using the test panel on the left
6.	Type "what time do you open" → bot should trigger this topic ✅
✅ Exercise 3: Create a Question Node + Variable
1.	In your topic, add a Question node after the message
2.	Question: "Which department do you need?"
3.	Options: "Sales", "Support", "Billing"
4.	The answer auto-saves to a variable (e.g., Var1)
5.	Add a Condition node: If Var1 = "Sales" → Message "Connecting to sales..."
6.	Test it → verify branching works
✅ Exercise 4: See Bot Variables vs Topic Variables
1.	Click on any variable in your topic → see Variable properties panel
2.	Toggle "Bot (global)" → this makes it a bot variable (persists across topics)
3.	Leave it OFF → it stays a topic variable (dies when topic ends)
4.	Create a SECOND topic → try to use the variable: 
o	Bot variable → ✅ appears in the second topic
o	Topic variable → ❌ does NOT appear
✅ Exercise 5: Suggest Topics from Website
1.	Go to Topics → Suggest topics
2.	Enter a URL: e.g., https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/ (or any FAQ page)
3.	Click Suggest → wait for extraction
4.	Review suggested topics → Add the ones you want → Enable them
5.	This is the exact 3-step process from Q176-177
✅ Exercise 6: Publish to Demo Website
1.	Go to Publish → click Publish
2.	After publishing, click Demo website link
3.	A new tab opens with your bot embedded → this is for testing/sharing with stakeholders
4.	Share this URL with a colleague → they can test without Teams
✅ Exercise 7: See Channels
1.	Go to Channels in the left menu
2.	You'll see: Microsoft Teams, Custom website, Facebook, Demo website, etc.
3.	Click Microsoft Teams → see the "Submit for admin approval" option (Q312-313)
4.	Click Custom website → see the embed code snippet (Q271)
