📘 TOPIC SHEET 6: Power Pages (Portals)
(12 questions — YOUR #2 WEAK AREA) ❌ Study from scratch
________________________________________
📖 Concept
Power Pages (formerly Power Apps Portals) = external-facing websites connected to Dataverse.
Core Security Model (EXAM LOVES THIS)
User visits website
    ↓
Authenticated? ──No──→ Anonymous Users Web Role (limited access)
    ↓ Yes
Which Web Role? ──→ Determines what pages + data they can access
    ↓
Page Permissions ──→ Controls which PAGES they can view
    ↓
Table Permissions ──→ Controls which DATA (records) they can read/write
    ↓
Scope of Table Permission:
    • Global = ALL records
    • Contact = only records linked to the user's contact
    • Account = only records linked to the user's account
    • Parent = only child records of a parent they have access to
    • Self = only the user's own contact record
Key Components
Component	What It Does	Exam Context
Web Role	Groups permissions together (like security roles)	Assign to users → controls access
Authenticated Users Role	Special flag on a web role → auto-assigned to ALL logged-in users	Set to true = every authenticated user gets this role
Table Permission	Controls CRUD access to Dataverse records	Scope: Global/Contact/Account/Parent/Self
Page Permission	Controls access to specific web pages	Restrict/Grant access to individual pages
Inherited Permissions	Child pages inherit parent page permissions	If disabled → child page is NOT accessible even if parent is
Identity Provider	How users authenticate	Local auth, Azure AD, Microsoft Account, Google, Facebook
Open Registration	Allow anyone to sign up	Enabled = public signup. Disabled = invitation only
________________________________________
🔑 Rules to Memorize
Rule	Remember
1	Authenticated Users Role = auto-assigned to ALL logged-in users when Authenticated Users Role = true
2	Anonymous users can ONLY see pages explicitly granted to the Anonymous Users web role
3	Table permissions control DATA access (records). Page permissions control PAGE access
4	Scope = Contact → user sees only records linked to their Contact record
5	Scope = Global → user sees ALL records (dangerous!)
6	Inherited permissions disabled → child pages are NOT accessible even if parent is ✅
7	Open Registration = disabled → users need an invitation code to register
8	Power Pages data source = ALWAYS Dataverse (no SQL, no Excel, no external)
9	Basic Form = single-step form. Advanced Form (Multi-step) = wizard-style form
10	Entity List (now List) = displays a grid of records on a page
________________________________________
📝 All Related Questions + Answers
Q5: Default permissions for students (free courses)
Scenario: Free courses auto-available after sign-in
Answer: ✅ C — Create entity for free courses → Create Students web role with Authenticated Users Role = true → Create entity permissions for free course records → assign to web role
❌ A — Assigning web role to each user individually = not scalable
❌ B — Creating entity permissions per user at registration = too manual
Key: Authenticated Users Role = true means ALL logged-in users get it automatically
________________________________________
Q115: Anonymous user can't view linked page
Scenario: Anonymous user sees Home page but NOT a linked child page
Answer: ✅ B. Inherited permissions are not enabled for the linked page
Why: If inherited permissions are OFF, the child page doesn't inherit the parent's access
❌ Authenticated Users Role — user is anonymous, not authenticated
❌ Maintenance mode — would block ALL pages, not just one
Key: Always check inherited permissions when child pages aren't visible
________________________________________
Q116: Authentication + permissions components
Requirements:
•	Only authenticated users sign in → Identity Provider (configure external auth like Azure AD)
•	Varying degrees of access → Web Roles (different roles for different access levels)
•	Select from external entities during registration → Entity Form with lookup fields
Key: Identity Provider + Web Roles + Entity Forms = the three pillars of portal security
________________________________________
Q120: Microsoft Account + invitation code authentication
Configuration:
•	External sign-in → Microsoft Account (identity provider)
•	Open Registration → Disabled (requires invitation code)
Key: Disabled open registration = invitation-only signup
________________________________________
Q123: User gets "permission denied" creating portal
Answer: ✅ A, C, E
•	A: User must have read-write access in Power Platform admin center
•	C: User must have permission to register an app in Azure AD
•	E: User must have System Administrator security role
Key: Portal creation requires both Power Platform admin permissions AND Azure AD app registration rights
________________________________________
Q124: Two communities (sales + service) with multiple languages
•	Languages for both → Enable language packs in the environment
•	Company logo/colors for all screens → Theme configuration
•	Separate communities with different URLs → Create separate portals (each gets its own URL)
________________________________________
Q183-184: Power Pages templates
•	Automated scheduling → Schedule and manage meetings template
•	Event registration → Community template (or custom)
•	Ticketing/support → Customer Self-Service template
Key: Know the main templates and their use cases
________________________________________
Q200: Webpage permissions setup
Scenario: Bellows College portal — set up page permissions for different pages
Key: Each page can have specific permissions controlling who can view/edit it
Combine Page Permissions + Web Roles for granular access
________________________________________
Q238: Portal email registration process
•	Send invitation code → Email (manual or automated)
•	User enters code during registration → Invitation entity in Dataverse
•	User signs in → Identity Provider validates credentials
Key: Invitation-based registration = Invitation entity + disabled open registration
________________________________________
Q256: Page permissions for store managers (data access)
Scenario: Managers must update stock for THEIR store only
Solution: Page permissions alone → ❌ No
Why: Page permissions control PAGE access, not DATA access. For record-level filtering (own store only), you need Table Permissions with Contact or Account scope
Key: Page permissions ≠ data-level security. Table permissions = data-level security
________________________________________
Q315: Power Pages data source
Answer: ✅ A. Microsoft Dataverse
Power Pages ONLY connects to Dataverse. No SQL Server, no Excel, no external databases
❌ Excel — not supported
❌ Azure SQL — not supported
❌ SQL Server — not supported
________________________________________
