📘 TOPIC SHEET 8: Forms (Main, Quick Create, Quick View, Card)
(~10 questions) ✅ You know the basics, but exam tests edge cases
________________________________________
📖 Concept
Form Type	Purpose	Where It Appears	User Can Create Records?
Main Form	Full data entry form	Opens when you click a record	✅ Yes (full edit)
Quick Create Form	Rapid entry with minimal fields	"+" button or quick create dialog	✅ Yes (minimal fields, no navigation away)
Quick View Form	Read-only snapshot from RELATED record	Embedded inside another form	❌ No (display only)
Card Form	Compact record summary	Board views, timeline, mobile	❌ No (display only)
🧠 Key Differences
Feature	Main	Quick Create	Quick View
Tabs/Sections	✅ Yes	❌ No (single section)	❌ No
Subgrids	✅ Yes	❌ No	❌ No
Business Rules	✅ Yes	✅ Yes	❌ No
Navigation away	Yes (opens full form)	❌ No (stays on current page)	N/A
Editable	✅ Yes	✅ Yes	❌ Read-only
Shows related data	Via subgrids/lookups	❌ No	✅ Yes (from parent/related)
________________________________________
🔑 Rules to Memorize
Rule	Remember
1	Quick Create = "rapidly create without navigating away" (exam keyword!)
2	Quick View = "display read-only data from a RELATED record"
3	Main Form = full editing, tabs, sections, subgrids, BPF, timeline
4	Card Form = compact summary in views/boards
5	Multiple Main Forms per table → controlled by form order or security role assignment
6	Quick View form requires a lookup relationship to the related table
7	To prepopulate data from related entity → Quick View Form
8	To let assistants edit data + see subgrids → Main Form
9	Form assignment: Settings → Form Order or Manage Roles per form
________________________________________
📝 All Related Questions + Answers
Q43: Embed related entity info + allow editing
Scenario: Main form doesn't show data from other entities
•	Embed read-only info from another entity → Quick View Form (add Quick View control)
•	Allow editing of related data → Add a subgrid (navigate to related records for editing)
Key: Quick View = read-only display. Subgrid = navigate + edit
________________________________________
Q77-78: Auto parts help desk — prepopulate + manual entry
Scenario: Prepopulate customer name from Client table + type automobile info
•	Prepopulate first/last name from Client → Quick View Form (displays Client data read-only)
•	Type automobile make/model → Main Form fields (editable text inputs on Automobile form)
________________________________________
Q91: Form types for different case types
Scenario: Different data entry needs for different case types
•	Minimal data entry, fast → Quick Create Form
•	Full details with all fields → Main Form
•	Summary card in list → Card Form
________________________________________
Q204: Bellows College — registration team vs assistants
•	Registration team: "rapidly create prospects without navigating away" + only First Name, Last Name, Birthdate → Quick Create Form
•	Assistants: "update prospect information and add teams to a subgrid" → Main Form
Key: "rapidly" + "without navigating away" = ALWAYS Quick Create. "subgrid" = ALWAYS Main Form
________________________________________
Q320-321: Embed custom interface in model-driven form without code
Answer: ✅ A. Create a canvas app and bind its properties to the form
Why: You can embed a canvas app inside a model-driven form → custom UI without code
❌ IFrame — requires HTML/code
❌ Quick View form — read-only, no custom interface
❌ Tablet form factor — changes layout, not custom interface
