🔧 Apply Section — Verify It Yourself
✅ Exercise 1: See All Form Types
1.	make.powerapps.com → Tables → Account → Forms
2.	Filter by form type → see: Main, Quick Create, Quick View, Card
3.	Open each one → notice the differences in layout/capabilities
✅ Exercise 2: Create a Quick Create Form
1.	Tables → Account → Forms → + New form → Quick Create Form
2.	Add ONLY 3-4 fields (e.g., Account Name, Phone, Email)
3.	Save & Publish
4.	Open a model-driven app → click "+" (quick create button) → select Account
5.	See your minimal form appear WITHOUT navigating away ✅
✅ Exercise 3: Create a Quick View Form
1.	Tables → Contact → Forms → + New form → Quick View Form
2.	Add: First Name, Last Name, Email
3.	Save & Publish
4.	Now go to Account → Main Form → add a Quick View control
5.	Select the Contact lookup → select your Quick View form
6.	Open an Account with a linked Contact → see Contact info displayed read-only
✅ Exercise 4: Embed Canvas App in Model-Driven Form
1.	Open Account → Main Form in form designer
2.	Click + Component → find Canvas App
3.	Create a new canvas app → it opens Power Apps Studio embedded
4.	Design your custom interface → Save & Publish
5.	Open Account form → see the canvas app embedded ✅
✅ Exercise 5: Form Assignment by Security Role
1.	Tables → Account → Forms
2.	If you have multiple Main Forms → click ⋯ → Form Settings
3.	See "Security Roles" tab → assign which roles see which form
4.	This is how different users see different forms for the same table
